ol_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "`payments-worker` is unhealthy on v3.4.0, and v3.3.0 is its most recent healthy production release. I'll roll it back to v3.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GURN4ox8kUU52DqzxG5Nhu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JnGAT1yJaGRHRWs9KWXTy5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "Payments errors following deploy: rolled back payments-worker to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "Payments errors began after this morning's deploy. payments-worker v3.4.0 was unhealthy in production (error rate 0.18) across us-east, us-west, and eu-west. Rolled back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production; rollout completed in all three regions. A rollback to payments-api v5.0.0 was attempted first and denied by a human reviewer as the wrong service; payments-api v5.1.0 is also reported unhealthy (error rate 0.18) and may need separate review. Follow-up: verify error rate recovery and investigate the v3.4.0 regression.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-sev2-2024-rollback-v3.4.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01KEsc4LuEEv3KZgcLiN5WnX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled back the service that was actually causing the errors, `payments-worker`, from v3.4.0 to v3.3.0. It is now healthy in all three production regions, with an error rate of 0.002. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Wrong service first:** \"payments\" wasn't a recognized service name. I found `payments-api` and rolled it back to v5.0.0, but a human reviewer denied that rollback and said the problem was in `payments-worker`. I didn't retry it.\n- **Rollback:** `payments-worker` v3.4.0 was unhealthy (error rate 0.18). I rolled it back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. That version needed no change-manager approval, and the reviewer approved it.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is SEV2 on `payments-worker`. The summary records the rollback, the denied `payments-api` attempt, and the follow-up work.\n\n`payments-api` is still on v5.1.0, which is reported unhealthy with an error rate of 0.18. I didn't change it. Someone should decide whether it needs its own rollback, since it may be contributing to the errors as well. The incident summary flags this.", "type": "text"}]}]}